{"ts": 1789783492.915406, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "This is the key result. The bar is 1.026 and my best is 0.831 \u2014 it does not clear.\n\nThe bar is *search-adjusted*: it accounts for the fact that I've run ~50 evaluations over a space of roughly 100,000 specifications. The whole point of that adjustment is that the maximum in-sample Sharpe from a wide search is inflated by selection. Let me quantify how much of my 0.831 is real.\n\nThe sign-flip tests above are informative: all three flips degrade heavily (0.831 \u2192 0.37, 0.25, 0.20), confirming the three features contribute consistently rather than one dominating. But consistency of contribution isn't the same as out-of-sample durability.\n\nLet me check whether the improvement from adding features is genuine diversification or just added flexibility to fit noise."}
